@OpenAI merged its standalone robotics team into its main research and applied groups, betting its general models can run robots.

In an @nvidia study, an agent built on GPT-6 Astra completed 74.8% of tasks on a simulated manipulation benchmark, beating the best robot-specific models at 51.0%.

Investors are betting the opposite way. In three weeks, @PathRobotics, Agile Robots and @BedrockRobotics raised $300 million, $500 million and $600 million for robots that work factory floors, warehouses and job sites.

@physical_int, which sells only a robot model, is in talks to raise at least $1 billion at a valuation of about $20 billion — the highest in the group.

@jasonjin2103 reports

